summary:
  The retry switch guards the ladder but not the directory lookup.

history:
  This is the bug 2026.37 actually shipped, found the day after. The switch
  was read in the one place the ladder arms, which looked like enough. It was
  not: a station that dies still reaches _tryHealStation, which asks the
  directory for its new address and starts playing it. Address healing is on
  by default, so the switch promised "a dead stream simply stops" and the
  stream came back anyway — the setting appearing to work while a different
  road undoes it is worse than no setting.

  Re-anchored 2026-09-18: both refusals now ask the shared _mayKnock,
  which is the structural answer to this bug rather than a second copy
  of the same condition.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
          // it is the one order the budget below never applies to.
          if (!_mayKnock(root._healRetryAttempts))
              return;

replace:
          // it is the one order the budget below never applies to.
          if (false)
              return;

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_the_retry_switch_also_covers_the_address_lookup.
  Line-neutral.
